WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:03.120
Yo, what's up? It's yoroomie, and in this video,

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:06.200
I'm going to talk to you about how I built a chatbot in hours.

00:00:06.279 --> 00:00:08.600
This is over the weekend.

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:13.100
Launched it and generated thousands of messages via this chatbot.

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:16.319
If you're interested in building your own chatbot, this video is for you.

00:00:16.319 --> 00:00:20.699
Let me talk to you a little bit more about why I built this chatbot.

00:00:20.699 --> 00:00:26.000
I've been someone that has been reading a lot about chatbots,

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:28.080
in literally--even on Chatbots Magazine.

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:31.799
I've seen BotList's Seth. He's the founder of BotList. He's incredible.

00:00:31.799 --> 00:00:37.000
I've seen all of his posts on, you know--I follow him on Facebook and on Twitter and everywhere.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:40.000
And I see all these chatbots that have been launched on product time.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:43.000
It was definitely something that I needed to learn more about,

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:47.200
and for me the easiest way to learn something is by immersing myself in that

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:51.000
and by building a side project and doing it.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:53.800
And my goal was not only learn about chatbots,

00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:57.629
but learn about the chatbot ecosystem and the tools that were out there.

00:00:57.629 --> 00:01:01.800
I found myself looking on an actual--on a browser window.

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:05.000
and I was looking at some artwork from an artist that I like--

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:06.200
Alec Monopoly.

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:08.900
So you might have seen some of his work.

00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:11.900
It's kind of like the monopoly man graffiti street art.

00:01:11.970 --> 00:01:15.689
But I'm pretty much obsessed a lot of his work and some other artworks,

00:01:15.689 --> 00:01:18.600
so I was like, "Why don't I build a chat bot

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:23.200
for people to discover artists' artwork and purchase all through messenger?"

00:01:23.229 --> 00:01:26.200
So I kind of come up with this, like, initial idea,

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:29.200
and just out of, like, the fact that I like artwork

00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:33.200
and that would be a cool way to get involved and combine my interest

00:01:33.250 --> 00:01:35.800
through this project of a chatbot.

00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:38.900
First off, it's like, all right, like, let's just start to Google

00:01:38.900 --> 00:01:40.900
and, you know, and look on Product Hunt

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:43.100
and see if there's any kind of art chat bot that's out there.

00:01:43.149 --> 00:01:47.579
Well, as I just said Art Chatbot, that's exactly how I came upon the name.

00:01:47.619 --> 00:01:53.000
So I immediately went to GoDaddy, and I typed in www.artchatbot.com

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:55.900
and to my surprise, man, it was available.

00:01:55.900 --> 00:01:59.810
So I click purchase on that. $9.99. I had the domain name.

00:01:59.810 --> 00:02:04.500
Just like with StudioTime, I used a Squarespace logo generator,

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:06.500
which is like a visual kind of logo creation tool,

00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:09.400
so I didn't have to use Photoshop.

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:13.600
I didn't have to use Sketch or any sophisticated design tool.

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:18.889
I simply used Squarespace's logo generator to generate the initial logo for Art Chatbot.

00:02:18.889 --> 00:02:22.039
So I had the name, domain, and logo.

00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:24.900
Now I needed to figure out: 
how am I actually gonna build this?

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:28.000
So I started researching some tools

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:32.689
and then also joining some of the chatbot developer groups on Facebook,

00:02:32.690 --> 00:02:35.100
which I can link down here to some of those

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:38.700
which are a huge resource in a lot of, you know, knowledge sharing going on

00:02:38.790 --> 00:02:40.800
But I found Chatfuel.

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:43.900
So Chatfuel is an easy way to create a chatbot,

00:02:43.900 --> 00:02:48.100
and it's basically a visual, kind of, chatbot creation platform,

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:51.600
and I started to just see what the other options were,

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:52.600
and I just said okay.

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:55.600
I'm just gonna commit to using chatfuel, learn how to use it.

00:02:55.600 --> 00:02:56.790
So I signed up for chatfuel.

00:02:56.790 --> 00:02:58.819
Super easy platform to use, by the way.

00:02:58.819 --> 00:03:01.879
They actually have templates that--that are on there

00:03:01.879 --> 00:03:06.800
so you can get started using a template  and modify it towards your needs.

00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:09.800
Now, once I created my account through chatfuel,

00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:12.800
and the Facebook page for Art Chatbot,

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:18.200
which I needed because that's how people were going to send a message to Art Chatbot,

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:20.959
I just, kind of, started using one of their placeholder templates,

00:03:20.959 --> 00:03:24.100
and I just understood from there

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:26.700
chatbots are all about conversation design.

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:32.000
So just like when you road--when you roadmap an app or even a website--

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:33.570
kind of the wire framing process--

00:03:33.570 --> 00:03:39.349
you can use that simple process to actually create the chatbot using chatfuel.

00:03:39.349 --> 00:03:42.000
So you can think about things like blocks,

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:44.800
and so when someone types an initial message,

00:03:44.850 --> 00:03:48.000
you know, this block then goes to a next block,

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:50.500
and you're gonna have different variable blocks

00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:54.100
to send them different messages or display other information,

00:03:54.100 --> 00:04:00.000
and then all of that together composes this kind of conversational design of the chatbot.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:01.700
It's really not that complicated.

00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:05.700
You know, to be honest, it's probably one of the easiest things I've ever built,

00:04:05.710 --> 00:04:07.710
and that's Art Chatbot.

00:04:07.710 --> 00:04:09.900
So within about 30 minutes,

00:04:09.900 --> 00:04:14.000
I had the initial template in place for Art Chatbot,

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:18.000
and I just started testing, real-time, the messaging on this,

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:23.000
and just started iterating the conversational design of what Art Chatbot would be

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:26.500
and what it actually is now in the stages it is live.

00:04:26.590 --> 00:04:30.600
And I'll link down here and screenshot, also, the website that I created

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:33.000
and you can actually test it out yourself

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:35.300
and let me know what you think and give me some feedback on it

00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:37.600
I'll, you know, obviously want to improve it.

00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:42.800
But you can kind of get a really good idea of that conversation design of Art Chatbot.

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:44.369
So in about 30 minutes to an hour,

00:04:44.370 --> 00:04:49.000
I had this initial version of the Art Chatbot actually built.

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:51.000
What I did from there was

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:56.000
I wanted to go ahead and get people to start using this.

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:59.900
What I did was I actually open-sourced most of the build.

00:04:59.900 --> 00:05:02.700
In doing that, I started to tweet about what I was doing.

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:08.300
I let people first off know, "Hey, I'm building a side project, Art Chatbot" on Twitter.

00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:12.100
I started to join and post in a lot of these groups

00:05:12.100 --> 00:05:15.209
for, you know, chatbot developers and chatbot communities on Facebook.

00:05:15.210 --> 00:05:17.210
I also shared on my personal Facebook.

00:05:17.290 --> 00:05:20.609
I also shared on my Instagram, which I'll link down here.

00:05:20.650 --> 00:05:24.479
It's @yoroomie, and then I also Instagramed stories.

00:05:24.479 --> 00:05:27.600
And I really showed people what I was doing.

00:05:27.600 --> 00:05:33.900
As I was doing that, people were becoming aware of this chatbot project that I was building.

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:37.100
They were giving me feedback, being involved in the process,

00:05:37.100 --> 00:05:39.700
and obviously once I had this ready to launch,

00:05:39.700 --> 00:05:44.000
some people already knew of what I was doing

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:48.800
and they were aware of it, and they had, kind of, participated in it in some sense in their mind.

00:05:48.880 --> 00:05:53.600
So I had some initial first users and an initial traction before I'd even launched.

00:05:53.600 --> 00:05:58.000
Keep in mind, this is literally within about the first hour to, you know, two hours.

00:05:58.000 --> 00:05:59.980
As I was going through this process

00:05:59.980 --> 00:06:04.109
and letting people know what I was doing and sharing more on the project,

00:06:04.110 --> 00:06:09.600
I also created a Google Doc where I was going to create a public product roadmap

00:06:09.600 --> 00:06:16.600
so people could contribute their feedback and their potential feature requests to this chatbot

00:06:16.660 --> 00:06:20.820
all via link and I created a bitly short link to that so I could send that,

00:06:20.820 --> 00:06:23.700
you know, on all my social and I could track that,

00:06:23.740 --> 00:06:26.500
but I wanted people to be involved in this project

00:06:26.500 --> 00:06:30.100
because if they were, then they were going to have some investment in the project

00:06:30.100 --> 00:06:32.100
and be more willing to probably share it

00:06:32.100 --> 00:06:35.800
and I could build some initial, kind of, traction and momentum as I launched.

00:06:35.800 --> 00:06:40.200
So people at this time were aware of what I was doing.

00:06:40.200 --> 00:06:42.989
They were giving me some feedback. I was, kind of, taking that feedback.

00:06:42.990 --> 00:06:45.100
I was adding it to the Google Doc.

00:06:45.100 --> 00:06:48.000
Then at the same time, I was being very open and honest

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:52.500
about how many users, you could say, the chatbot had

00:06:52.500 --> 00:06:54.780
and then the amount of messages that it was sending.

00:06:54.780 --> 00:07:00.000
So I was sharing the analytics, and that is actually something that is interesting to a lot of people.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:03.200
What I found out is people want to know, you know,

00:07:03.200 --> 00:07:05.800
not only in the process of how you build these things,

00:07:05.800 --> 00:07:09.100
but also, like, how do you actually launch these

00:07:09.100 --> 00:07:11.100
and how effective are the launches?

00:07:11.100 --> 00:07:15.200
Are people messaging it? If so, what are the actual analytics like?

00:07:15.200 --> 00:07:19.000
So these--these are things that typically startups don't share as much,

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:22.489
so I was being open and honest and open sourcing most of this,

00:07:22.489 --> 00:07:25.100
which was actually its own, kind of, angle of interest

00:07:25.100 --> 00:07:28.000
that people started becoming interested in.

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:31.000
So at that time, I had initial chatbot built,

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:37.100
and I had an initial, kind of, community around this that I had created in the first users.

00:07:37.100 --> 00:07:41.500
One of the biggest objectives for having a chatbot website

00:07:41.580 --> 00:07:46.100
is not only to let people know about what the chatbot is and the functionality

00:07:46.139 --> 00:07:48.400
but simply to get people to message it

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:53.200
because once you send a message to a chatbot, that is technically considered a user.

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:56.000
And I'll just use air quotes because that's, you know, loosely defined.

00:07:56.010 --> 00:07:59.000
But that is an opt-in. That's considered a user.

00:07:59.000 --> 00:08:04.000
And for analytics, that starts the messages that are counted as messages that you send out.

00:08:04.050 --> 00:08:09.229
I'll link to it down here, and I'll screenshot with you the current website,

00:08:09.229 --> 00:08:13.000
but it is www.artchatbot.com.

00:08:13.050 --> 00:08:19.200
But as you can see I just simply have the name, the logo, the tagline.

00:08:19.200 --> 00:08:22.200
I have a large button that's the call to action,

00:08:22.200 --> 00:08:25.700
then I have a visual image of the Art Chatbot,

00:08:25.700 --> 00:08:28.400
and some of the artwork that's displayed,

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:30.470
and then also at the very bottom in the footer,

00:08:30.470 --> 00:08:35.150
I do have a link to that open source Google Doc

00:08:35.150 --> 00:08:40.000
so people that come to the site can not only see Art Chatbot,

00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:41.520
not only send it a message,

00:08:41.520 --> 00:08:42.800
but be aware of,

00:08:42.800 --> 00:08:46.500
"hey, you can contribute your feedback to Art Chatbot

00:08:46.500 --> 00:08:51.800
and you can see the analytics real-time, kind of, open source of this project

00:08:51.800 --> 00:08:53.730
and stay up to date and in the loop with this."

00:08:53.730 --> 00:08:57.600
I've actually found that there's been thousands of hits to that Google Doc

00:08:57.600 --> 00:09:02.539
and a lot of people are very interested in how many messages are being sent too

00:09:02.539 --> 00:09:04.500
and contributing to this.

00:09:04.500 --> 00:09:05.500
So it's just been a really cool project for me,

00:09:05.500 --> 00:09:08.400
and not only have I learned a lot about chatbots--

00:09:08.459 --> 00:09:13.000
you know, built out a network of other chatbot developers,

00:09:13.000 --> 00:09:16.000
of people that are working on, you know, building chatbot, kind of, tools--

00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:18.000
the developer ecosystem--

00:09:18.000 --> 00:09:23.930
but also, too, perfecting my process of not only how do I approach side projects, but how do I build them?

00:09:23.930 --> 00:09:26.000
How do I market them?

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:30.500
How do I share more information about these projects to people?

00:09:30.500 --> 00:09:34.900
And then also learning, what are people interested in, you know, seeing with these side projects?

00:09:34.900 --> 00:09:36.300
And really sharing it.

00:09:36.350 --> 00:09:38.100
So that's one of the biggest things that I like doing

00:09:38.100 --> 00:09:40.100
is just being open and honest

00:09:40.100 --> 00:09:44.000
and open sourcing a lot of these side projects and sharing with people.

00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:47.200
Hopefully you know a little bit more about Art Chatbot,

00:09:47.200 --> 00:09:49.100
how I'm approaching chatbots,

00:09:49.100 --> 00:09:51.210
and how I got started building this,

00:09:51.210 --> 00:09:53.100
how effective it's been.

